{
  "result": "execscale_census_note",
  "date": "2026-10-12",
  "question": "which of the census's 58 committed programmes does HEAD no longer match, and which commit moved each one?",
  "claim": "a byte comparison and a git attribution, nothing else: every programme of data/results/execscale_census.json against its bytes on disk now, and for each difference the commits after 81d3949 that touched that path. The census is not rewritten. NOTHING about the magnitude, nothing about RNA, nothing fitted.",
  "does_not_claim": "it says nothing about whether a change was correct, nothing about RNA, and nothing about the magnitude the census was taken for; it fits nothing and reads no measurement",
  "readings": {
    "the_census_record_is_sound": "its group_sha256 is exactly reproducible from the 58 blobs at 81d3949 in the record's own order, and every per-file digest matches those blobs. The record is a record of one tree and that tree still answers for it. tests/test_execscale_rescoped.py::test_the_recorded_group_digest_is_REPRODUCIBLE_from_the_tree_it_was_taken_on is the check.",
    "the_two_group_digest_implementations_agree": "manifest.group_digest and the duplicate at scripts/execscale_census.py:125 return the same digest for the same list in the same order, on the committed group of 58 programmes. The duplicate is NOT removed here: removing it is a removal inside a check_staged window, so it is reported for the timed list instead.",
    "a_group_digest_carries_the_LIST_as_well_as_the_CONTENT": "both implementations hash name + b'\\0' + bytes per member IN THE ORDER GIVEN and neither sorts internally, so membership and order move the digest while no per-file digest moves. The 58 per-file digests alone therefore do not carry the census's claim: a programme added, removed or reordered is invisible to them. And because manifest.files_entry SORTS its names before hashing while execscale_census.programs() concatenates per-tree sorted lists over three trees, the two routes to a group's digest disagree by construction -- which is how a checker can report that only the group digest differs on a tree whose every per-file digest matches."
  },
